{"t": 1792880713164, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "chron1", "PASS epitaph: Greenshire took Upperwood's (my) last village at tick 18003 after the 12-round siege. Chronicle (Y) epitaph: 'The banners of Upperwood came down when Greenshire took its last village.' Fits: it was a village, the conqueror is named correctly, no 'never raised a hut' text. Same for Cityton/Castlefield at 18251. Note: the preceding 'After a siege, a village of Upperwood fell to Greenshire.' entry is missing from the 'Your news' view (only the epitaph shows there)."]}
{"t": 1792880713478, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "conquered", "Major ux: when MY nation was conquered (tick 18003) the status line only said 'Autosaved.'; no 'Greenshire took your village - Upperwood is no more' status. 248 ticks later the status announced 'Cityton has fallen and been disbanded.' - a stranger's nation gets a status line, mine does not. The HUD silently flips to Nation: none, Create/Join Nation buttons, and a red unexplained 'Collapsing! 4:40 left' era timer. Objective 5 still says 'Enter your settlement' though I no longer have one."]}
